      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T03:34:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my opinion; yes. However, here the intent is to directly match the values coming from AVB, and in the documentation / property list this value is listed as a string which is either \"locked\" or \"unlocked\".\n\nI assume there\u0027s probably a good reason for that where I\u0027m lacking some context that David or Shawn could fill in. If I had to guess, it\u0027s either that some third value could be possible in future releases, or that it\u0027s harder for a developer to accidentally invert the meaning of a string than the meaning of a boolean, so it\u0027s better to err on the side of caution when a mistake means revoking attestation keys.",
      "parentUuid": "57e2fd4f_979fa9d1",
